The 'styles/hud' folder holds the CSS modules for the theme-registry's shell components (apps/game-client/src/components/hud/), originally introduced by the 2026-09-14 custom-hud-layout plan for the compact layout specifically. It establishes the baseline/untheme visual look for BOTH of slate-amber's shells — desktop (CompactLayoutShell.module.scss: terminal panel with an embedded title via the shared borderedPanelTitle mixin, vitals gauges, room row, plugin widget slots, two-column split) and narrow (CompactLayoutShellNarrow.module.scss: the same rows single-column, plus a Chat/Affects tab strip) — while exposing plain `sa-hud-*` global class hooks on the rendered elements so an opt-in theme can repaint them without depending on Vite's hashed CSS-module class names. `themes/slateAmber.theme.scss` is that opt-in theme — a global side-effect import (not CSS Modules) gated behind `:root[data-hud-theme='slate-amber']`, imported directly by both shells so it bundles into whichever one's chunk actually loads; features/hudLayout/themeRegistry.ts's `loadStyles` sets the attribute, nothing else. Per the design spec (§4.3), the baseline module always owns a working default appearance — a theme only ever layers on top, never supplies the only color.
